diff --git a/docs/mcp-runtime-lifecycle.md b/docs/mcp-runtime-lifecycle.md
index 0fea07026a..fea2defe3a 100644
--- a/docs/mcp-runtime-lifecycle.md
+++ b/docs/mcp-runtime-lifecycle.md
@@ -100,6 +100,7 @@ For each discovered server in `connectServers()`:
 - creates stdio or HTTP/SSE transport,
 - performs MCP `initialize` using protocol version `2025-11-25` and advertises the `roots` capability,
 - answers server-to-client `ping` and `roots/list` requests; unsupported request methods return JSON-RPC `-32601`,
+- for sessions with a screen, also advertises form `elicitation` and answers `elicitation/create` through `ElicitationBroker` (`src/mcp/elicitation.ts`) one question at a time, using the session's `askDialog` (the dialog the `ask` tool uses, no timeout). A request with no fields (an approval such as "may I run this action?") is one `Accept`/`Decline` question: Accept answers `accept`, Decline answers `decline`. A request with fields is one question per field (boolean → Yes/No, enum → its choices, multi-select array → a multi-choice question, string/number → the dialog's free-text row) plus a final `Submit this form?` Accept/Decline question; invalid answers are asked again for those fields only, up to five dialogs. Everything else, including a dismissed dialog, "chat about this", a timed-out item, mismatched results, an `askDialog`-less host or a thrown error, answers `cancel`; it is never read as acceptance. URL mode returns `-32602`,
 - sends `notifications/initialized` before any further session traffic,
 - for Streamable HTTP, starts the background SSE listener only after `notifications/initialized`,
 - uses timeout precedence `OMP_MCP_TIMEOUT_MS`, then `config.timeout`, then 30s; `0` disables the client-side timeout,
